.\" consoleuser(8) -- NextBSD (nextbsd-userland#199)
.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt CONSOLEUSER 8
.Os NextBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm consoleuser
.Nd publish the console user in the dynamic store
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /usr/libexec/consoleuser
.Cm set Ar user
.Nm /usr/libexec/consoleuser
.Cm clear
.Nm /usr/libexec/consoleuser
.Cm show
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
writes, removes or prints the
.Li State:/Users/ConsoleUser
key of the
.Xr configd 8
dynamic store: the user logged in at the console, with the
.Li Name ,
.Li UID ,
.Li GID
and
.Li SessionInfo
properties Apple's loginwindow publishes through
.Fn SCDynamicStoreSetConsoleInformation .
A login program runs
.Cm set
after the user's session opens and
.Cm clear
after it ends.
.Pp
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
watches the key.
At a login, removable and external volumes mount owned by the console user,
who may also unmount and eject them; at the logout the user's volumes are
unmounted and their disks ejected.
NextBSD ships
.Pa /Local/Library/Preferences/SystemConfiguration/autodiskmount.plist
with
.Li AutomountDisksWithoutUserLogin
set, so such media also mount, owned by root, while nobody is logged in.
Removing that key once a login program runs
.Nm
gives Apple's behaviour: the media wait for a login.
.Bl -tag -width "clear"
.It Cm set Ar user
Publish
.Ar user ,
looked up with
.Xr getpwnam 3 ,
as the console user with one console session.
Root only.
.It Cm clear
Remove the key; nobody is logged in.
Root only.
.It Cm show
Print the console user's name, uid, gid and session count, or
.Dq none .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr configd 8 ,
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8 ,
.Xr scutil 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in NextBSD as the console-user publisher for
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8 .
